  "title": "Thumb under",
  "summary": "Going past five keys: the right thumb tucks under.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Fingering",
      "body": "**Fingering**: the plan for which finger plays each key. Music prints it as small finger numbers over the notes.\n\n**Why it matters:** five fingers run out quickly. A good plan lets you keep going smoothly, where a poor one leaves you stuck with no finger for the next key.",
      "hands": [
        {
          "hand": "right",
          "keys": [
            60,
            62,
            64,
            65,
            67
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Thumb under",
      "body": "**Thumb under**: going up with the right hand, after finger 3 plays, the thumb slides under fingers 2 and 3 to the next key, and the whole hand moves along to follow it.\n\n**Why it matters:** it carries a run of notes past five keys with no gap or jump, which is how scales are played.\n\nPress **Watch**: C, D, E with fingers 1, 2, 3, then the thumb tucks under to F and the hand moves over.",
      "hands": [
        {
